                <pb facs="0955" n="875" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg875"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Merry.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic">March 14,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hill states that a delay of thirty days to present proofs for the
                    arbitration of the Gelbtrunk claim in form requested by Salvador is granted;
                    that this action closes the agreement to arbitrate the claim, and that proofs
                    will accordingly be presented.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
